## Week 1: Infrastructure + CRD Foundation

### Day 1-2: Lab Network Setup (DEN080)

IMPORTANT: Before anything else, connect to lab VPN and verify firmware:
- SSH to admin machine (10.80.18.102)
- Pick a test server, access its iDRAC/BMC console
- Run efibootmgr (or check BIOS boot menu) to confirm "UEFI PXEv6" boot entry exists
- If PXEv6 is missing, check firmware update options before proceeding

Network tasks:
- [ ] Choose an unused VLAN ID (check https://quip-amazon.com/ArLuA3HDsLSK for inventory)
- [ ] Assign a ULA IPv6 prefix: e.g. fd00:80:66::/64
- [ ] Create VLAN on all switches via manage_vlans.sh on ns2.den080.eksalab.net
- [ ] Configure SVI on distribution switch(es):
      - Assign IPv6 address to SVI (e.g. fd00:80:66::1/64 as gateway)
      - Suppress RAs: `ipv6 nd suppress-ra` (smee is authoritative, no SLAAC)
      - OR send minimal RA with M-flag set (managed-config) if iPXE needs RA to bootstrap DHCPv6
- [ ] Assign 4-5 server access ports to the new VLAN
- [ ] Configure admin machine (10.80.18.102) with an IPv6 address on the new VLAN:
      - If trunk port: add tagged VLAN interface (e.g. eth0.VLAN_ID with fd00:80:66::2/64)
      - If access port: may need a second NIC or reconfigure
- [ ] Verify IPv6 connectivity: ping6 between admin machine and switch SVI

### Day 2-3: CRD Patch (Upstream PR #445)

- [ ] Review upstream PR https://github.com/tinkerbell/tinkerbell/pull/445 diff
- [ ] Cherry-pick or replicate the IPv6 CRD field additions locally:
      - Expected: prefix_length field in interface.dhcp.ip (or new ipv6 block)
      - Validate: do the new fields cover what DHCPv6 IA_NA needs? (address + prefix length minimum)
- [ ] Apply patched CRD to local crd/bases/tinkerbell.org_hardware.yaml
- [ ] Update Go types in api/v1alpha1 if needed to match CRD schema changes
- [ ] Verify: `go build ./...` passes with the new fields

