## Week 3: Lab Testing + Debugging

### Day 8-9: Deploy and First Boot Attempt

- [ ] Build modified smee binary (or container image)
- [ ] Deploy standalone tink stack to k3d on admin machine:
      k3d cluster create --network host --no-lb --k3s-arg "--disable=traefik,servicelb,metrics-server,local-storage"
      helm install tink-stack (with patched CRDs)
- [ ] Create Hardware object for test server:
      - MAC: (PXE NIC MAC on IPv6 VLAN)
      - IP address: fd00:80:66::10 (or similar)
      - prefix_length: 64
      - gateway: fd00:80:66::1
      - Netboot.AllowPXE: true
- [ ] Set test server boot order to PXEv6 via iDRAC/IPMI:
      ipmitool -H <bmc_ip> -U <user> -P <pass> -I lanplus chassis bootdev pxe options=efiboot
      (may need to specifically select the PXEv6 boot entry via efibootmgr or BIOS)
- [ ] Power on test server, watch console via iDRAC virtual console
- [ ] Monitor smee logs for incoming DHCPv6 Solicit

### Day 9-11: Debug Loop

Expected issues to troubleshoot:
- [ ] iPXE not sending DHCPv6 Solicit: may need minimal RA with M-flag
      - Workaround: configure radvd on admin machine or switch SVI to send RA with managed-config flag
- [ ] DHCPv6 option 59 (boot file URL) not being parsed by iPXE
      - Check iPXE source/docs for expected option format
      - May need to use option 60 (bootfile-param) additionally
- [ ] iPXE chainload loop: ensure UserClass "Tinkerbell" detection works over DHCPv6
      - DHCPv6 option 15 (User Class) vs DHCPv4 option 77
- [ ] Kernel/initrd download fails: verify HTTP server on admin machine is listening on IPv6
      - k3d with --network host should expose on all interfaces including IPv6
- [ ] iPXE hangs at "Waiting for link-up": physical cabling / VLAN mismatch

### Day 11-12: Validate End-to-End + Document

- [ ] Confirm HookOS boots and shows login prompt on iDRAC console
- [ ] Capture packet trace (tcpdump on admin machine) showing full DHCPv6 exchange
- [ ] Document:
      - What CRD fields were needed (feedback for upstream PR #445)
      - Any iPXE quirks discovered (RA requirement, option format, etc.)
      - Network topology that worked
      - Firmware requirements / known-good server models

